Run JMeter from this directory with `jmeter` on PATH and a running Solr
instance. Open SolrQueryTest.jmx to see the Test Plan parameters, including
serverName and serverPort.

Pass JMeter properties with -J (the plan reads them with __P). queryFile
must name a query corpus, not a corpus alias. The default is the retained
field.queries file beside the plan; an explicit absolute path avoids
working-directory ambiguity. Create the results directory before running:

$ mkdir -p test
$ jmeter -n -t SolrQueryTest.jmx -JbaseDir="$PWD/test" -JdurationInSecs=5 -JrampUpInSecs=0 -JqueryFile="$PWD/field.queries"

The other retained corpora are queries.txt, citation_queries.txt and
ads_classic_queries.csv. Select one by passing its path with -JqueryFile.
